  "name": "The Paleogeography and Climatic History of Beringia During Late Cenozoic Time",
  "description": "Beringia has played a strategic role in the evolution of northern biota during late Cenozoic time, because of it's position athwart restrictions in both intercontinental and interhemispheric dispersal routes. [Reference: Hopkins, D.M., 1972, The paleogeograhy and climatic history of Beringia during late Cenozoic time: International Journal of Arctic and Nordic Studies, v. 12, p. 121-150.]\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To record the paleogeography and climatic history of Beringia during late Cenozoic time.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23563612",
